CloseCaseRequest.description:
``POST /cases/{id}/close``: the analyst's delegated close.

``plain_summary`` is what the PO reads, so it must be in business words;
the route refuses one that names a score, band or rating.

JurisdictionVersionOut.description:
``GET /jurisdictions/versions``: one stored jurisdiction list version.
``fixture`` marks a synthetic test list (never an FATF publication);
``active`` is the one list new work is checked against.

OutcomeRecord.description:
``POST /outcomes`` (service). ``committee`` records what a tallied pack
decided (``pack_id`` required, the outcome must be the tallied one);
``delegated`` records an analyst's close under R1 (no pack, a reason).

SimulateResponse.description:
Both scores of the control's domain and of the case, with the band and
the boundary flag each time. The first five pairs are the web's contract;
``route``, ``boundary_flag`` and ``boundary_distance`` are additive.
